    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0721" n="617" xml:id="pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of
                        War Mobilization</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Byrnes</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d385-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-28">November 28, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Extensive studies of various problems required before decision can be
                        reached.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d385-f2"/> In meantime you should proceed as
                    before the question of increase in landing craft was raised.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d385-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d385-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Washington via military channels, and forwarded by the White House Map
                    Room to Byrnes.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d385-f2" n="2" xml:id="d385-f2-content">
                <p>See Byrnes’ telegrams of November 24 and 27, 1943, <ref target="#pg395">pp.
                        395</ref> and <ref target="#pg444">444</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
